        <mxCell id="sKme" value="&lt;b&gt;KME&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br&gt;This site's key source,&lt;br&gt;on the internet" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#d5e8d4;strokeColor=#82b366;fontSize=14;" vertex="1" parent="sae">
          <mxGeometry x="600" y="48" width="360" height="90" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="sSame" value="&lt;b&gt;Second SAE&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br&gt;The same design.&lt;br&gt;Own identity, database, and KME." style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#f3eaf7;strokeColor=#9673a6;fontSize=14;dashed=1;" vertex="1" parent="sae">
          <mxGeometry x="600" y="170" width="360" height="100" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="sSteps" value="&lt;b&gt;Install&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;1. Bring up an HSM on the site network and initialize it for this node.&lt;br&gt;2. Create the node's identity on the HSM, and the trust anchors. Import this site's KME client key.&lt;br&gt;3. Install the SAE directory. Every site holds the same copy, and each node is pinned in it. The file stays mode 0644 or stricter.&lt;br&gt;4. Open the firewall as drawn. Other SAEs may reach this registry port and that port plus 40000. Every node adds 40000; the offset is fixed in the software.&lt;br&gt;This node may reach its KME. The HSM stays on the site network.&lt;br&gt;5. Create this site's database. The node creates the file mode 0600, owner read and write only.&lt;br&gt;6. Start the node. The operator works at its console.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;The second SAE repeats these steps." style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#9673a6;fontSize=13;align=left;spacingLeft=10;spacingRight=8;" vertex="1" parent="sae">
          <mxGeometry x="16" y="368" width="948" height="290" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>

